COMMENT     The assembly wsSpiGran1.hap1.1 is based on 133x PacBio data and
            Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Aquatic Symbiosis Genomics
            Project (https://www.aquaticsymbiosisgenomics.org/). The assembly
            process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio
            assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode,
            and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was
            assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was
            analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale
            scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of
            size. This assembly contains a number if heterozygous inversions.
            Chromosome 1 -
            85,250 - 86,750 Mbp. Chromosome 2 -
            44,350-49,200 Mbp. Chromosome 6 - a number of reciprocal
            rearrangements between 4,300 and 12,200 Mbp. Chromosome 7 - 9,300 -
            13,650 Mbp. Chromosome 10 -
            7,700-13,500 Mbp. Chromosome 12 - a number of rearrangements
            between
            8,600-17,600 Mbp.
